sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-acetabularia-acetabulum-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-acetabularia-acetabulum-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-acetabularia-acetabulum-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Acetabularia acetabulum Turing wavelength at 25.28 µm (Holocene, detail scale) — MorphoEval overall 85.4/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1. Brusselator on a periodic cap-wall patch with D_u = 10.20 µm²/s and D_v = 122.4 µm²/s. Onset wavelength 22.67 µm, fastest linear mode 25.43 µm, saturated FFT peak 25.08 µm against the tier length 25.28 µm (2.528e-5 m, 0 Ma). Dispersion Pearson r = 0.9996 (RMSE 0.016 /s). Equal-diffusion ablation decays (amplitude ratio 0.097). First face-on GIF scored CV 82.0 against the CC0 cap before speckle was added. Anisotropy was still a single constant (0.45). Overall 85.4/100 (faithfulness 84.3, reproducibility 87.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit bd2c74bc; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.x, note Cloud agent VM; no project venv. Cryptographic nanopub signing unavailable (~/.nanopub/profile.yml absent).. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 80, Morphometric validation 86, Source and data traceability 91, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/acetabularia_acetabulum_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-acetabularia-acetabulum-turing-wavelength-s0.py at bd2c74bc, image/gif, 4027264 B, 640×480 px, 12 frames, artifact_sha256 48f30bdef7c6420215c169bc392f46857a15535c9cf793a90b0b70b33c03e8c9 (sha256 48f30bdef7c6420215c169bc392f46857a15535c9cf793a90b0b70b33c03e8c9), spec_fingerprint 96087cd4e2bc623a26b35d593a33788c367131953ba2d7b731f791fb3ce2cc1b. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 96087cd4e2bc623a26b35d593a33788c367131953ba2d7b731f791fb3ce2cc1b; artifact_sha256: 48f30bdef7c6420215c169bc392f46857a15535c9cf793a90b0b70b33c03e8c9; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/acetabularia_acetabulum_turing_wavelength_s0/acetabularia_acetabulum_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=3e562916ba2ad34f..., datasets/acetabularia_acetabulum_turing_wavelength_s0/acetabularia_acetabulum_wikimedia_cc0.jpg=0773237a26517128...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability and the critical wavenumber. | Dumais & Harrison 2000: Acetabularia whorls are the pattern for which reaction-diffusion is the mechanism the experiments favour. | Holloway & Harrison 2007: a Brusselator on a growing plant surface produces whorled branches.; reconstructed_in_script: Nominal A, B and diffusivities that place the fastest mode on the 25.28 µm tier length. | Inhibitor axial/hoop diffusivity ratio 0.45, which selects axial ridges. | Face-on tiling of the periodic patch into an 88-ridge young cap of radius 354 µm.; transfer_boundary: 25.28 µm is the MorphoEval tier length, not a spacing measured by Dumais & Harrison. | The CC0 photograph is an adult cap; the model cap is the 0.71 mm disk implied by 88 ridges at 25.28 µm.; does_not_claim: That the gallery plate or the CC0 photograph is a calibrated micrograph of 25.28 µm pigment stripes. | A successor chronospecies. The Acetabularia series in this slot is Holocene only. | That sibling slot 192 parameters were reused.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [parameter_sweep/parameter-expressivity, pressure P=1.7]: Sweep D_axial/D_hoop and record which Fourier axis wins.",
            "open need [specimen_comparison/specimen-match, pressure P=1.5]: Bring rendered structure-tensor coherency toward the CC0 cap without copying its pixels.",
            "remediation needed: Second assessor from another provider has not scored this audit.",
            "remediation needed: Sweep the inhibitor axial/hoop ratio and show the handoff from hoop-dominated ridges to axial waves.",
            "remediation needed: The adult CC0 cap is not metrically registered to the 0.71 mm model disk.",
            "remediation needed: The first render is smoother than the sand-speckled CC0 cap; add seeded grain so coherency is not systematically higher than the specimen." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.854"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor; second assessor not run)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

